<html>
  <head>
    <meta http-equiv="Content-Type" content="text/html; charset=Cp1252">
    <meta name="generator" content="Helen">
    <link rel="stylesheet" type="text/css" href="../../../../javahelp.css">
    <title>Modifying the zoom scale from the dialog window</title>
  </head>
  <body bgcolor="#ffffff">
    <h1>
       <img border="0" hspace="0" s7starttagpos="303" height="32" width="32" src=
      "../../../../images/carmenHelpIcons/c3_32.gif">&nbsp;&nbsp; Modifying the zoom scale from the
      dialog window
    </h1>
    <table border="1" cellpadding="4" cellspacing="0" bordercolor="#000000" width="490">
      <col width="234">
      <col width="238">
      <tr>
        <td colspan="2" valign="top" width="480">
          <p align="left">
             <b><font size="3">Use case: Modifying the zoom scale from the dialog window</font></b>
          </p>
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td colspan="2" valign="top" width="480">
          <p align="justify">
             <b><font size="3">Comment:</font></b> <font size="3">The user is able to change the
            scale factor through two magnifying glass buttons located on the standard toolbar or on
            the main menu. These buttons increase or decrease the scale factor by 20%,
            respectively. The description of the way to do can be seen in the table.</font>
          </p>
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td colspan="2" valign="top" width="480">
          <p align="left">
             <b><font size="3">Actor: User</font></b>
          </p>
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr valign="top">
        <td width="234">
          <p align="left">
             <b><font size="3">Normal course</font></b>
          </p>
        </td>
        <td width="238">
          <p align="left">
             <b><font size="3">Alternative courses</font></b>
          </p>
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr valign="top">
        <td width="234">
          <p align="justify">
             <font size="3">1.The user selects from the main menu the option to change the scale
            factor using a box dialog.</font>
          </p>
        </td>
        <td width="238">
          <p style=" margin-left: 1.25cm; margin-right: -0.02cm; text-indent: -0.79cm;" align=
          "justify">
             <font size="3"><br>
            </font>
          </p>
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr valign="top">
        <td width="234">
          <p align="justify">
             <font size="3">2.The program displays a dialog box with a fixed set of scaling factors
            to be chosen by the user and a text box where you can type an integer value between 10
            and 500.</font>
          </p>
        </td>
        <td width="238">
          <p style=" margin-left: 1.25cm; margin-right: -0.02cm; text-indent: -0.79cm;" align=
          "justify">
             <font size="3"><br>
            </font>
          </p>
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr valign="top">
        <td width="234">
          <p align="justify">
             <font size="3">3.The user chooses the desired value or types a new value.</font>
          </p>
        </td>
        <td width="238">
          <p align="justify">
             <font size="3">3.1.If the user does not want to change the scale factor, he/she
            cancels the operation, ending the use case.</font>
          </p>
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr valign="top">
        <td width="234">
          <p align="justify">
             <font size="3">4.The program checks the value chosen by the user.</font>
          </p>
        </td>
        <td width="238">
          <p align="justify">
             <font size="3">4.1.If the user has decided to type a value and the value is not
            correct, the program will report the fact and will go back to point 3.</font>
          </p>
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr valign="top">
        <td width="234">
          <p align="justify">
             <font size="3">5.It continues from point 3 of the use case <i>Modifying the zoom
            scale</i>.</font>
          </p>
        </td>
        <td width="238">
          <p style=" margin-left: 1.25cm; margin-right: -0.02cm; text-indent: -0.79cm;" align=
          "justify">
             <font size="3"><br>
            </font>
          </p>
        </td>
      </tr>
    </table>
  </body>
</html>
